.TH XPROXY\-FLEET 8 "" "Xproxy" "System administration"
.nh
.ad l
.SH "NAME"
.PP
xproxy\-fleet \- fleet controller: configuration bundles and status for many xproxy nodes
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.PP
\fBxproxy\-fleet serve\fR \fB\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR \fB\-listen\fR \fIADDR\fR \fB\-cert\fR \fIPEM\fR \fB\-key\fR \fIPEM\fR \fB\-ca\fR \fIPEM\fR [\fB\-any\-name\fR] [\fB\-scan\fR \fID\fR] [\fB\-admin\-socket\fR \fIPATH\fR]
.PP
\fBxproxy\-fleet nodes\fR [\fB\-admin\-socket\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-json\fR]
.PP
\fBxproxy\-fleet node\fR \fIID\fR [\fB\-admin\-socket\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-json\fR]
.PP
\fBxproxy\-fleet bundle\fR \fIID\fR [\fB\-admin\-socket\fR \fIPATH\fR]
.PP
\fBxproxy\-fleet scan\fR [\fB\-admin\-socket\fR \fIPATH\fR]
.PP
\fBxproxy\-fleet validate\fR [\fB\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR]
.PP
\fBxproxy\-fleet version\fR
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
\fBxproxy\-fleet\fR runs on a management host. Every \fBxproxy\fR(8) node with a \fBfleet\fR section long polls it for the configuration bundle assigned to the node and reports its status; the controller never connects to a node. The directory holds:
.PP
.TS
allbox;
lbw(1.2i) lbx
lw(1.2i) lx.
T{
Path
T}	T{
Content
T}
T{
\fIDIR\fR\fB/\:common/\fR
T}	T{
Files every node receives
T}
T{
\fIDIR\fR\fB/\:nodes/\fR*ID*\fB/\fR
T}	T{
A node\(aqs own files,\: overriding common ones;\: \fBxproxy.\:yaml\fR is its configuration
T}
T{
\fIDIR\fR\fB/\:status/\fR
T}	T{
The last report per node,\: kept across restarts
T}
T{
\fIDIR\fR\fB/\:fleet.\:sock\fR
T}	T{
The operator socket the query commands use
T}
.TE
.PP
Editing the files is the push: the controller rescans every \fB\-scan\fR interval, a bundle whose files no longer parse is not served (the last good one stays and the error shows in \fBnodes\fR), and the agents apply a changed bundle within seconds through the ordinary reload path, rolling back the files when the proxy refuses the configuration.
.PP
Agents authenticate with a client certificate from \fB\-ca\fR; the certificate\(aqs common name or DNS name must equal the node id unless \fB\-any\-name\fR is given.
